# Bugfix: Disable Station/Shot Interactions for Zoom and Pan Tools

## Problem

When Zoom or Pan tool is active, users can still:
- Click to select stations/shots
- See hover effects (stroke width/color changes) on stations/shots
- Right-click to open context menu on stations/shots
- Trigger keyboard shortcuts for selection (Ctrl+A, Delete/Backspace)

This is confusing because these tools should only allow zoom/pan operations, not feature interactions.

## Approach

Disable all station/shot interactions when `activeTool` is `'zoom'` or `'pan'`:

### 1. Define NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS constant

```typescript
// In uiStore.ts (around line 20, after ToolType)
export const NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS: ToolType[] = ['pan', 'zoom'];
```

### 2. useMapTools.ts - Add early returns

Check tool at start of each handler:

```typescript
// Line 76 - handleStationClick
const handleStationClick = useCallback((ref, event) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing switch statement
}, [activeTool, ...]);

// Line 187 - handleShotClick
const handleShotClick = useCallback((sectionId, shotId, event) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing logic
}, [activeTool, ...]);

// Line 301 - handleStationHover
const handleStationHover = useCallback((ref) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) {
    setHoveredStation(null);
    return;
  }
  setHoveredStation(ref);
}, [activeTool, setHoveredStation]);

// Line 309 - handleShotHover
const handleShotHover = useCallback((shot) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) {
    setHoveredShot(null);
    return;
  }
  setHoveredShot(shot);
}, [activeTool, setHoveredShot]);

// Line 317 - handleContextMenu
const handleContextMenu = useCallback((target, event) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing logic
}, [activeTool, ...]);
```

### 3. SurveyLayer.tsx - Add setActiveTool method

```typescript
import { NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS, ToolType } from '../../store/uiStore';

private activeTool: ToolType = 'select';

public setActiveTool(tool: ToolType): void {
  const wasNonInteractive = NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(this.activeTool);
  const isNonInteractive = NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(tool);

  this.activeTool = tool;

  // Clear hover when switching to non-interactive tool
  if (!wasNonInteractive && isNonInteractive) {
    this.hoveredStationId = null;
    this.hoveredShotId = null;
    this.updateVisualState();
    this.map.getCanvas().style.cursor = '';
  }
}
```

Update mouseenter handlers (lines 449 and 478) to check tool:
```typescript
this.map.on('mouseenter', this.stationsLayerId, (e) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(this.activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing logic (cursor change, hover state, callbacks)
});

this.map.on('mouseenter', this.shotsLayerId, (e) => {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(this.activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing logic
});
```

### 4. MapCanvas.tsx - Wire up setActiveTool

Add useEffect after line 579 (after callbacks useEffect):
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (surveyLayerRef.current) {
    surveyLayerRef.current.setActiveTool(activeTool);
  }
}, [activeTool]);
```

### 5. useKeyboardShortcuts.ts - Disable selection shortcuts

```typescript
// Line 114 - Ctrl+A select all
case 'a':
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) return;
  event.preventDefault();
  // ... existing logic

// Line 193 - Delete/Backspace
if (key === 'delete' || key === 'backspace') {
  if (NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS.includes(activeTool)) return;
  // ... existing logic
}
```

### 6. Cursor behavior

- Don't change cursor to 'pointer' when hovering features with non-interactive tools
- Keep default cursor or tool-specific cursor (grab for pan, zoom-in for zoom)
- The early return in SurveyLayer mouseenter handlers prevents cursor change naturally

### 7. Edge Cases

- **Tool switch while hovering**: Clear hover immediately via setActiveTool
- **Selection persists**: Keep existing selection when switching to pan/zoom (don't clear)
- **Keyboard shortcuts**: Disable Ctrl+A and Delete/Backspace when pan/zoom active

## Files to Modify

1. `src/store/uiStore.ts` - Add NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS constant (line ~20)
2. `src/hooks/useMapTools.ts` - Add early returns in all handlers (lines 76, 187, 301, 309, 317)
3. `src/components/Map/SurveyLayer.tsx` - Add setActiveTool, update mouseenter handlers (lines 449, 478)
4. `src/components/Map/MapCanvas.tsx` - Wire up setActiveTool useEffect (after line 579)
5. `src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` - Disable shortcuts for pan/zoom (lines 114, 193)
6. `docs/keyboard-shortcuts.md` - Document behavior
7. `CHANGELOG.md` - Note the bugfix

## Quick Commands

```bash
# Type check
pnpm tsc --noEmit

# Run tests
pnpm test:ui
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] NON_INTERACTIVE_TOOLS constant defined with 'pan' and 'zoom'
- [ ] Click on station/shot does nothing when Zoom/Pan active
- [ ] Hover effects (stroke width/color) don't appear when Zoom/Pan active
- [ ] Right-click context menu doesn't open when Zoom/Pan active
- [ ] Cursor stays default (not pointer) when hovering features with Zoom/Pan
- [ ] Switching to Zoom/Pan clears any current hover state
- [ ] Existing selection persists when switching to Zoom/Pan
- [ ] Ctrl+A (select all) disabled when Zoom/Pan active
- [ ] Delete/Backspace shortcuts disabled when Zoom/Pan active
- [ ] E2E tests verify Zoom/Pan don't allow selection
- [ ] Unit tests verify useMapTools handlers return early
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] `pnpm tsc --noEmit` passes
- [ ] All tests pass

